Three primary issues fall for consideration in the present case, which are as follows:
(I) Whether the appellant-wife is guilty of mental cruelty towards the respondent-husband and his family;
(IIA) Whether the marriage between the parties has broken down irretrievably;
(IIB) Whether such irretrievable breakdown can be a ground for divorce; (III)
Whether the learned Trial Judge ought to have granted permanent alimony.
26.
